{
  "$comment": "Shared nightly job list. Every project in config/projects.json runs every job whose `requires` capabilities it has (scripts/lib/nightlyPlan.js), unless config/projects/<slug>.json declares nightly.waivers.<jobId> with a reason. `providers` is the order a job's scripts try data sources (cheapest first; 'alchemy' last). `alchemyOnly` jobs have no free source and are skipped, not degraded, when the Alchemy budget is spent. `alchemyCuPerNight` is the per-project per-run budget the rpc.js guard enforces (HD_JOB_ALCHEMY_CU_BUDGET); config/budgets.json keeps the monthly ceiling. `outputs[].maxAgeHours` is the freshness SLA pipeline-health.js checks; paths are TEL-layout and are mapped per project (public/data/<f> -> <dataDir>/<f>, data/<f> -> data/<slug>/<f>). `budgetMode`: 'enforce' = the guard refuses Alchemy calls past the budget (next provider, or skip for alchemyOnly); 'warn' = it only logs ::warning:: and records the overrun (used where a hard stop could leave a feed stale; tighten to enforce once the job has run within budget for a month). `dataset`: the data set a job produces; the parity test (scripts/lib/nightlyPlan.test.js) requires every project to run, or explicitly waive, at least one job per dataset (chain-specific variants such as staker-balances / solana-staking share a dataset). Per project, scripts/lib/nightlyPlan.js providersFor() drops 'alchemy' when the project has no EVM chain (Alchemy serves no Solana chain here) and 'helius' when it has no Solana chain.",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
